The scheduler picks the latest deadline on the run queue rather than the earliest.
A thread with an earlier deadline starves on the run queue while threads with later deadlines run.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a thread waits with a deadline before the turn's request
Witness: fuzz time-edf-order

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -576,7 +576,7 @@ static struct place *run_earliest(const struct core *core)
     for (paddr_t at = best->queue_next; at != core->run_queue;) {
         LOOP_BOUND(TIME_UNITS);
         struct place *p = p2v(at);
-        if (tick_before(p->deadline, best->deadline)) {
+        if (!tick_before(p->deadline, best->deadline)) {
             best = p;
         }
         at = p->queue_next;
